# Data Security

This rule outlines the security requirements and best practices for the Summer to Remember application.

## Authentication & Authorization

- Use OAuth 2.0 for secure authentication with Google services
- Implement secure token management including storage and refresh mechanisms
- Ensure tokens are scoped with minimal necessary permissions (calendar, tasks, and photos access only)
- Store authentication tokens securely using appropriate methods for your platform

## Data Protection

- Store user data securely, following best practices for your chosen data storage system
- Implement proper access controls to ensure users can only access their own data
- Minimize sensitive data storage on the client side
- Ensure all API calls are made securely over HTTPS

## Implementation Requirements

- All API calls must use secure connections
- Implement appropriate error handling for authentication failures
- Regular security audits should be performed on the codebase
- Follow the principle of least privilege when requesting access to user data
## Google API Specific Security

- Configure Google Cloud project with appropriate security settings
- Set up OAuth consent screen correctly with minimal required scopes
- For Google Photos API, ensure proper scope configuration to prevent 403 errors
- Implement token deletion/re-authentication flow when updating required scopes

Remember that data security is an ongoing process that requires regular review and updates as the application evolves.
